Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-17-2000||08:54 PM||||Click on the link to view the pictures from the show. It was only a mini show with the members from the Suncoast Fiero Club (of which I will soon be a member). This club did VERY well at the 2000 Daytona show.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=446733&a=7224351" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=446733&a=7224351</A> <P>Enjoy,<BR>Roy||||reg||6
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||07-17-2000||10:07 PM||||Nice looking club Mr.fixit Tell us about the speakers in the V8 car???<P>Lots of custom work, how many member?<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-18-2000||07:24 AM||||Not much to tell about the speakers... I'm really not much of an audiophile. I do know that he had this big bass box in the floorboard on the passenger's side. It sure looked uncomfortable but his girlfriend didnt seem to mind. If your really interested and can provide me with the questions, I'll pass them alon at the next meeting.<P>The club is about eight months old and has over 30 members. It will soon have two more, me and my Bro-in-law. They gave each of us a copy of their last news letter and it was one of the best I've seen.<P>Althought this was a small showing at a relitively small show, their main purpose for participating was the officers wanted to meet the man doing the trophy presentations. He is the same one working the BIG Daytona show for 2001. The club seems very well organized.<P>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||07-18-2000||09:06 AM||||Nice, nice Fieros, especially that 86 GT w/ V8.<P>But please tell me those are some kind of show registration slips under the wipers and not parking tickets... <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=446733&a=7224351&p=24553151" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=446733&a=7224351&p=24553151</A> ||||reg||14
